###Writing an equation

Let's substitute $\blueE{24}$ for $\blueE{\text{area}}$. Then, we can solve for $\maroonD{\text{length }(l)}$ in terms of $\goldE{\text{width }(w)}$:

$\begin{align}
\blueE{\text{area}} &= (\maroonD{\text{length}}) \cdot (\goldE{\text{width}})
\\\\
\blueE{24} &= \maroonD{l} \cdot \goldE{w}
\\\\
\dfrac{\blueE{24}}{\goldE{w}} &= \maroonD{l}
\\\\
\maroonD{l} &= \dfrac{\blueE{24}}{\goldE{w}}
\end{align}$

###Length when width is $2.5$ meters?

Let's use our equation to find the value of $\maroonD{l}$ when $\goldE{w}=\goldE{2.5}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{l} &= \dfrac{\blueE{24}}{\goldE{w}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\blueE{24}}{\goldE{2.5}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{48}{5}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{96}{10}
\\\\
&=9.6
\end{align}$
